{"id":"ecb8dda9db7aa32dc9adeacbed006750a58934bb","axis":"silent","repo":"apache/tika","sha":"ecb8dda9db7aa32dc9adeacbed006750a58934bb","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"CHANGES.txt","lines":["@@ -24,6 +24,10 @@ Release 4.2.0 - unreleased","      Every resolver Tika installs answers with an empty stream, never null (TIKA-4941).","    * Deprecate XMLReaderUtils.getXMLInputFactory() and use SAX for XFA (TIKA-4938)."," ","+   * Quiet default pipes logging: per-parse timing lines (WORKER/CLIENT/","+     SERVER/RESOURCE_TIMING) move from INFO to TRACE, and per-fork-start,","+     per-connection and plugin lifecycle lines move to DEBUG (TIKA-4949).","+"," Release 4.1.0 - 9/26/2026"," ","   HIGHLIGHTS"],"additions":4,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/modules/ROOT/pages/pipes/troubleshooting.adoc","lines":["@@ -230,6 +230,8 @@ Your file overrides the bundled one entirely. Start from a copy of the bundled c"," "," Forked PipesServer JVMs get their own config, not the parent's: unless `forkedJvmArgs` already carries a `-Dlog4j.configurationFile` / `-Dlog4j2.configurationFile`, the parent adds `-Dlog4j.configurationFile=classpath:pipes-fork-server-default-log4j2.xml`. What reaches your terminal is separately governed by `tika.pipes.server.stdio` — set it to `discard` and all fork stdout/stderr is suppressed at the OS level (see <<_configuration_knobs_reference,Configuration knobs reference>>)."," ","+Per-parse timing lines log at `TRACE` on `org.apache.tika.pipes.timing`: `CLIENT_TIMING` (and, in tika-server, `SERVER_TIMING`/`RESOURCE_TIMING`) from the parent, `WORKER_TIMING` from the fork. Enabling the logger in the parent's config does not reach the fork; for worker lines, copy `pipes-fork-server-default-log4j2.xml`, uncomment its timing logger, and pass it via `forkedJvmArgs`.","+"," To debug a specific fork, leave stdio on `inherit` (the default) and grep parent log output for the `pipesClientId=<n>` marker that each fork includes."," "," == Configuration knobs refer